resses in <italic>Caulobacter crescentus</italic></article-title><source>J Bacteriol</source><year>2005</year><volume>187</volume><fpage>8437</fpage><lpage>8449</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16321948</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b27"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Izawa</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Importance of glucose-6-phosphate dehydrogenase in the adaptive response to hydrogen peroxide in <italic>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</italic></article-title><source>Biochem J</source><year>1998</year><volume>330</volume><fpage>811</fpage><lpage>817</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9480895</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b28"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jung</surname><given-names>IL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Abnormal growth of polyamine-deficient <italic>Escherichia coli</italic> mutant is partially caused by oxidative stress-induced damage</article-title><source>Arch Biochem Biophys</source><year>2003</year><volume>418</volume><fpage>125</fpage><lpage>132</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14522584</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b29"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Macaskie</surname><given-names>LE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>An immobilized cell bioprocess for the removal of heavy metals from aqueous flows</article-title><source>J Chem Technol Biotechnol</source><year>1990</year><volume>49</volume><fpage>357</fpage><lpage>379</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1366967</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b30"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Macaskie</surname><given-names>LE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cadmium removal by micro-organisms</article-title><source>Environ Technol Lett</source><year>1982</year><volume>3</volume>